Description: vf_inlineass: introduce SubCueClock primitive for bitmap path
 The bitmap path (PGS/DVD/DVB) carried its own ad-hoc display-window state
 (have_bmp, bmp_start_ms, bmp_end_ms, bmp_pend_start_ms, bmp_pend_end_ms)
 with the lifecycle scattered across replay_bitmap (decoder thread) and
 refresh_bitmap (filter thread). The window was open-ended for PGS cues
 (end_display_time=0 -> sentinel -1) and a previous patch (0121, now
 dropped) had to add an explicit close-on-clear fix because the per-frame
 recompute would otherwise resurrect a just-cleared cue.
 .
 Consolidate the lifecycle into a small SubCueClock primitive with three
 inline ops: sub_cue_set, sub_cue_close, sub_cue_active_at. INT64_MIN is
 the open-ended sentinel. close() always bounds the window, so the
 sticky-clear behaviour is enforced by the API rather than by remembering
 to write bmp_end_ms = time_ms at every clear site.
 .
 Net effect:
   - Folds 5 scattered fields into 2 (bmp_clock + bmp_pend_clock).
   - Single source of truth for "is the bitmap cue active at T".
   - Patch 0121's sticky-clear fix is absorbed (file removed alongside).
   - No behaviour change for the text path (libass owns its own clock).
   - No perf delta: same compare-and-cache, just behind an inline.
   - Text path could adopt the primitive later (e.g. to gate
     animated_tier_down windows); not retrofitted here to keep the
     diff scoped.
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-05-27

